Z||000000||GodSend||09-11-2000||09:19 AM||||  I am midly entertaining the idea of putting 2 rods of neon under the old beast - I checked the archive and could not come up with any solid answers. (I only want one 2 footer in the front and one 2 footer in the rear - under the car)<P>a] I know these babies are supposed to be shatter proof - but exatly HOW shatter proof - Are they fairly easily to break, or do they take alot?<P>b] My car is not a winter driver (will be off the road mid november to early april) - but otherwise how do these things hold upto Canadian weather?<P>c) Legal in Ontario?<BR><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.hypernetcommunications.com/revn.gif"> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||myblack86GT||09-11-2000||05:37 PM||||I have 2 tubes of Neon on my 86GT, but I put them on the sides, I scrape the front to much to put it there. I used 4-foot rods on the sides. I drive on gravel roads at high speed, and I havent broken one yet. If you hit them on somthing (ex. the curb or somthing you drive over) they will brake, so you have to be careful. And as far as holding up well, mine do, I drive this car all winter, and they have done good the last 2 years. Just make sure the clamps that hold them to the car allow them some give, because if they dont, and you hit a big bump, it could bust them. BTW, mine are Aqua.||||reg||1
